{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/767645-wording-an-oath-of-hospitality","id":767645,"title":"Wording an Oath of Hospitality","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-17T01:09:22-08:00","id":767645,"title":"Wording an Oath of Hospitality","content":"Our group usually don't pay much attention to the details of an oath. The few times they make one, they have no intention to break it. When dealing with NPCs the exact effects are usually not particularly important. One of these standard assumptions is a small Oath of Hospitality during large gatherings, effective for a the duration of the feast and dealing with non-hostility. Summer Court is now hosting a specific event, and the players are seriously contemplating the use of violence. I am looking for some word smiths to create a simple Oath of Hospitality for the guests not to use violence except in the dueling ring and in self-defense. It is an oath from the perspective of the guests, and obviously there should be an appropriate punishment mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T15:32:11-08:00","id":768139,"title":"","content":"How tightly worded do you want this pledge to be? The sort of thing they'd really have to work to circumvent, or the sort of thing with loopholes you could fly the USS Enterprise through?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T20:59:41-08:00","id":768271,"title":"","content":"&quot;Should guest strike guest, guest strike host, or host strike guest, they shall not rest for one year and one day.&quot;<br /> <br /> - That leaves things pretty open to interpretation (do gunshots count as a &quot;strike&quot;?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T02:13:25-08:00","id":768362,"title":"","content":"Somewhere in the middle, although it should be noted that it would be a relatively traditional type of oath designed by experienced Summer Courtiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T21:16:50-08:00","id":768934,"title":"","content":"&quot;I promise I'll be a good guest as long as you're a good host. I'll keep violence in the ring where it belongs, unless someone else attacks first. In exchange, &lt;boons&gt;. If I break my word, Everyone here's welcome to beat on me all they want - I'd deserve it!&quot;<br /> <br /> Task: Minor forbiddance (Don't break the rules of hospitality) -1 <br /> Task: Minor forbiddance (Don't start a fight outside the listed bounds) -1 <br /> Duration: As needed (+1-3)<br /> Boons: As needed (+1-3)<br /> Sanction: Vulnerability (violence) -2<br /> <br /> The total from Duration and Boons must equal +4, unless you consider either of the Forbiddances to be Medial rather than Minor,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T03:29:01-08:00","id":769072,"title":"","content":"I would use something along those lines:<br /> <br /> &quot; We vow to not use violence against each other, except when such violence is confined within the boundaries of the ring. In return, [boons]. Should one of us breaks his world, he shall be defenceless against our wrath. Be it known that this pact has been sealed and will be enforced for [duration].<br /> <br /> Type of pledge: Group Vow.<br /> Task: Medial Forbiddance (-2)<br /> Sanction: Violence OR Glamour Vulnerability (-2).<br /> Boon: Your choice (+1 to +3).<br /> Duration: Your choice (+1 to +3), but something like \u201cuntil the end of the event\u201d should be avoided, because we don't know how to rate such a variable duration.<br /> <br /> <br /> Note and possible loopholes:<br /> <br /> - Everybody must be present to seal this pledge (cost: 1 Willpower from the main Host). Bringing somebody else into the pledge afterwards will cost 1 Willpower for all pledgers, and all of them must again be present. The characters might want to act before the pledge is sealed, or they might want to infiltrate the event.<br /> <br /> - The obvious loophole is that only violence against somebody part of the pledge is banned. Violence against objects, or somebody not part of the pledge, is allowed.<br /> <br /> - The characters may trick the Host into breaking the pledge using the ring. (What if a part of the body is outside the area? How high does the area extend above the ground? Can somebody inside the ring attack somebody outside it? Is it a violation of the &quot;violence confined within the boundaries of the ring&quot; clause if somebody inside the ring causes one of your character to be ejected outside the ring? \u2026)<br /> <br /> - The pledge lasts for the stated duration, but the actual event might last shorter or longer. This can be an opportunity to trick someone into believing that the pledge is no longer in effect, or take advantage on the fact that the pledge is no longer in effect while the event is still going on.<br /> <br /> - And of course, there is always the Oathbreaker's Honesty (from the \u201cLords of Summer\u201d rulebook).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9493-enmai","name":"Enmai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T03:47:15-08:00","id":772203,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I went with the one by Enmai. The players decided to stick to the Oath, but their discussion about it and the loopholes was interesting. They didn't go for the bait, which disappointed one of their enemies. For the curious, they knew about a planned assassination attempt and the debate was whether to proactively strike or wait for the right moment. They picked the last. They concluded they had too little evidence to make it stick, and in the end did not care enough about the NPC for the risk of failing to stop it on time. They should be a bit more paranoid though, because instead of rushing the assassin out of the building for questioning they did it right in front of the wrong people <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}